Subject: [PATCH] VIF1: lite transfers - no UNPACK into VU1 memory, no programs, while the port asks

ps2vif1::setLite(predicate): while it answers true (asked once per transfer), VIF1 leaves
out the work only VU1's programs use: an UNPACK writes nothing into VU1 data memory and
MSCAL / MSCALF / MSCNT start no program (TOP / ITOP / DBF bookkeeping as before). MPG,
DIRECT / DIRECTHL, the registers, MARK and the interrupts are unchanged. For a port whose
renderer draws from the display list in main memory and in which nothing reads VU1's
results (Transformers roadmap N5.2). Null predicate (the default): nothing changes.

ps2vif1::setLiteScan(predicate): the same for the scan of each transfer on the EE's
thread. Answering 1, the GIF data of DIRECT is not walked (its GS registers only serve
the readbacks ahead of the queue; those are answered the plain way meanwhile and for 120
readbacks after); interrupts and MARK as before. Answering 3, the same, and the scan done
on the VIF1 thread as the transfer comes up instead of on the EE's before it is queued:
the interrupts and MARK come when VIF1 gets there (as on the console), VIF1_STAT / MARK
read what it has got to (g_scan under a lock; a scan back on the EE's thread first waits
for the pending ones). Answering 2, walked as before on the EE's thread, but the readbacks
met and the EE's VIF1_STAT / MARK reads with a transfer still queued are counted (a check
mode). Null (the default): nothing changes.

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_vif1_thread.h b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_vif1_thread.h
index e6894d5..78f1cfe 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_vif1_thread.h
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_vif1_thread.h
@@ -88,6 +88,23 @@ namespace ps2vif1
     bool readUnobserved(uint32_t physicalAddress, uint32_t bytes, uint32_t &value);
     bool writeUnobserved(PS2Memory &memory, uint32_t physicalAddress, uint32_t bytes, uint32_t value);
 
+    // Lite transfers (the game port's choice: Transformers' roadmap N5.2). While the predicate answers true - a native
+    // renderer draws everything from the display list in main memory, and nothing reads what VU1 makes of it - VIF1
+    // leaves out the work that only VU1's programs use: an UNPACK writes nothing into VU1 data memory, and MSCAL /
+    // MSCALF / MSCNT start no program (their TOP / ITOP / DBF bookkeeping as before). MPG, DIRECT / DIRECTHL (the GIF),
+    // the registers, MARK and the interrupts are as before. Asked once per transfer. Null (the default): never.
+    void setLite(bool (*predicate)());
+    bool liteNow();
+    // The same for the scan of each transfer on the EE's thread (before it is queued): while the predicate answers 1, the
+    // GIF data of DIRECT is not walked - its GS registers only serve the readbacks ahead of the queue, and those are
+    // answered the plain way meanwhile (and for a while after it: until the registers are known again). The interrupts
+    // and MARK as before. 2: walked as before, but counted as if lite (the port's check mode): the readbacks met then,
+    // and the EE's reads of VIF1_STAT / VIF1_MARK while a transfer was still queued. 3: as 1, and the scan done on the
+    // VIF1 thread as the transfer comes up, not on the EE's before it is queued - the interrupts and MARK then come
+    // when VIF1 gets to the transfer (as on the console), and VIF1_STAT / VIF1_MARK read what it has got to.
+    // Asked once per transfer. Null (the default): never.
+    void setLiteScan(int (*predicate)());
+
     // How far the thread is in the transfer it is processing (the interpreter reports it).
     void progress(uint32_t offsetInTransfer);
 
